claimed: okay-script-storefront-example -- the worked runtime-storefront example filed in BACKLOG after okay-script-runtime/okay-script-lifecycle landed. A .md file (content pulled from ../it-consulting/site/site.md -- the real IT-consulting services list: name/description/price/currency in Russian) whose scala blocks start a real okay-jetty server rendering a storefront page + an /order route, compiled and run end to end through ScalaScript.run using the proven lifecycle recipe (own Thread, Thread.interrupt() to stop). No busi/scalascript DSL reused -- only the service DATA, expressed as plain Scala.
